    "Part of melonDS DS." : {
      "comment" : "Origin of a library on the Licenses screen."
    },
    "Part of melonDS DS. Arcfold switches its network emulation off. Further files of libslirp built into Arcfold are under these terms with these copyright lines: Copyright (c) 2013 Guillaume Subiron, Yann Bordenave, Serigne Modou Wagne; Copyright 2016 Thomas Huth, Red Hat Inc.; Copyright Gavin Shan, IBM Corporation 2016; Copyright (C) 2016-2018 IBM Corp." : {
      "comment" : "Origin and further copyright holders of libslirp on the Licenses screen. Keep the names and years."
    },
    "Part of melonDS DS. Of the libraries pntr brings along, Arcfold builds stb_image, stb_image_write, stb_truetype and font8x8 and uses them under their public-domain terms." : {
      "comment" : "Origin of pntr and the libraries it bundles, on the Licenses screen. Keep the library names."
    },
    "Part of melonDS DS. Source code: github.com/melonDS-emu/melonDS, commit 906e9eb. It includes SHA-1 in C by Steve Reid, which is in the public domain. On 7 November 2026 Arcfold removed the DSi's key material from it: the AES key of boot2, the key X of modcrypt and of the key slots, the eMMC keys and the key scrambler constant. Arcfold runs only the DS mode, which needs none of them. The change is in Scripts/cores/melondsds.sh in Arcfold's source code." : {
      "comment" : "Where the source of melonDS is and how Arcfold changed it, on the Licenses screen. Keep the address, the commit, the date and the file path."
    },
    "Part of melonDS." : {
      "comment" : "Origin of a library on the Licenses screen."
    },
    "Part of melonDS: the replacement for the console's BIOS that lets Arcfold start DS games without BIOS files." : {
      "comment" : "Origin of FreeBIOS on the Licenses screen."
    },
